      "keyFacts": [
        "Standards: I.S. EN 50600-3-1 + Uptime M&O Operational Sustainability",
        "Procedures: Complete vetted SOP (Routine), EOP (Emergency), MOP (Switching)",
        "Drills: Live Black-Hat failure simulations (utility outage, cooling/fire failure)",
        "Staffing: 24/7/365 Critical Facilities team trained & competency-certified pre-COD",
        "Spares: 2-year strategic OEM critical spares + 4h/24h SLA contracts active"
      ],
      "readme": "# PM-32: Operational Readiness & Transition (OR&T) & Black-Hat Drills\n\n- **Phase**: `Phase 6: Handover, OR&T & Closeout (RIBA 6-7)`\n- **RIBA Stage**: `RIBA Stage 6`\n- **P6 Milestone Gate**: `A6510-A6540`\n- **WBS Scope**: `WBS 6.5-OPS`\n- **Governing Standards**: I.S. EN 50600-3-1 M&O, Uptime Operational Sustainability\n- **Focus Areas**: SOP / EOP / MOP Library, Black-Hat Outage Drills, 24/7 Crew Competency, OEM Critical SLAs, 2-Yr Spares Inventory\n\n## Module Overview\nTrain 24/7 Critical Facilities staff, validate EOP/MOP/SOP libraries, run live Black-Hat incident drills, and stock 2-year critical spares.\n\n## Ordered Flashcard Documents (`Doc 1` -> `Doc 4`)\n\n| Doc | Category | Title | Exact Local File | Companion / Notes |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Doc 1 | Standard | I.S. EN 50600-3-1 Management & Operations + Uptime Operational Sustainability | `PM32_Doc1_Standard_I_S_EN_50600_3_1_Management_Rev.004.docx` | EN 50600-3-1 / Uptime M&O |\n| Doc 2 | Deliverable | Critical Facilities Operations Handbook: EOP, MOP & SOP Playbook Library | `PM32_Doc2_Deliverable_Critical_Facilities_Operations_Rev.004.docx` | Stage 6 OR&T Runbooks |\n| Doc 3 | Template | Live Black-Hat Unannounced Outage Drill Scripts & 24/7 Crew Scorecards | `PM32_Doc3_Template_Live_Black_Hat_Unannounced_Outage_Rev.004.xlsx` | Operator Drill Simulation |\n| Doc 4 | Audit | 24/7 Technician Competency Sign-Offs, OEM SLAs & 2-Year Critical Spares Log | `PM32_Doc4_Audit_24_7_Technician_Competency_Sign_Rev.004.xlsx` | Spares & Competency Check |\n\n## Study Takeaway (`Why Each Document Matters`)\n- **Doc 1 (Standard)**: Avoid human-error outages (>70% of failures) through certified operating discipline.\n- **Doc 2 (Deliverable)**: Equip shift engineers with step-by-step switching and emergency response guides.\n- **Doc 3 (Template)**: Test live crew reactions to simulated tripped breakers, chiller leaks, and fire alarms.\n- **Doc 4 (Audit)**: Ensure breakers, PLC cards, fan drives, and 4-hour vendor SLAs exist prior to Day-1.\n",
